    "status": "experimental-public-api-not-conformance-evidence",
    "notes": "This portable C++ TCK slice joins a subject with one non-universal directed interaction subscription under each of two adapter-selected object classes, each paired with its FOM-defined directed interaction class. A distinct requester subscribes to the standard MIM report interactions and requests the subject's subscriptions. The reports must identify both object-class groups and their corresponding directed interaction classes. After the standard set-based unsubscribe removes the primary object-class group, a second request must report only the remaining secondary group. The scenario uses only official IEEE 1516.1 RTIambassador and FederateAmbassador APIs, the standard MIM, standard encoding DataElements, and the C++ standard library. Provider package, FOM modules, endpoint, callback configuration, class names, and logical-time implementation come from the adapter. No DDM regions, private headers, provider registry, or vendor-specific API are used.",
